components.responsibility:
Walk_ItemDeleted_ClimbsToParent (ShellRevealTests.cs:139-156) is replaced by fake-seam tests:
- the parse returns 0x80070002: the outcome is Failed/NoLongerExists, the recording open delegate is never called, and no second parse happens;
- the parse returns 0x80070005: Failed with that HRESULT, not NoLongerExists;
- the parse returns S_OK and the open returns E_FAIL: Failed with E_FAIL, no retry, one parse.

One real-tree test, Walk_OnRealTree_RefusesGoneTargetsAndLandsThePresentOne, builds a %TEMP% tree holding gone\victim.bin, a deleted leaf in a surviving parent, and a present sibling. It deletes as needed, then runs Walk with the real SHParseDisplayName on an STA thread, as RevealAsync does, and a recording open. It asserts:
- both gone shapes give NoLongerExists and no open call;
- the present sibling parses S_OK and reaches the recording open exactly once.

Without that last check, a parse broken in testhost (COM not initialised, for example) would pass 'open never called' vacuously. No window is opened. The test runs in the default suite.

Wait-ExplorerSelection (WindowCases.ps1:3304-3318) no longer compares literal or lower-cased paths. A new Resolve-LongPath helper resolves both sides: Add-Type GetLongPathNameW on a \\?\-prefixed path with a 32767-char buffer, prefix stripped.

A landing matches when some ShellWindows entry meets all three conditions:
- its resolved Document.Folder.Self.Path equals the target's parent (OrdinalIgnoreCase);
- SelectedItems().Count is exactly 1;
- that item's resolved Path equals the target.

Name is logged, and asserted as well for folder targets (criterion 1). Windows are polled every 25 ms. Every entry is considered, because Explorer reuses a window already on the parent (spike case B).

Adds fields to the hook's existing reveal log line, only where they are missing:
- revealStartQpc, taken with Stopwatch.GetTimestamp() in a class-level PreviewExecuted handler for the Open in Explorer command;
- the outcome's kind, reason and HRESULT;
- the status text shown.

The schema-1 --report output is not changed. The hook is outside FsAnalyser.slnx and is built only by Update-Hook, so the build must run Update-Hook through eng/dotnet.ps1 explicitly and grep the hook for 'Ancestor'. Otherwise a compile break, or a string-based reference to the deleted kind, stays hidden until validate.

Records three things:
- SL-088 reverses SL-047's nearest-ancestor fallback under criterion 6;
- Hidden+System targets are knowingly out of this slice while their spike waits on a person;
- the product still reports Exact from hr==0, and only the window tests check the landing (criterion 4).

contracts.error_cases:
The case fails on any of these:
- no matching window within 1000 ms on a timed step;
- a selection count other than 1;
- a resolved folder or selection other than the one expected;
- a fixture-root window left open before a step;
- a Deny-All fixture that can still be enumerated;
- a new #32770 window owned by explorer.exe or the app, or a consent.exe process;
- any new or re-navigated Explorer window during the deleted-parent step;
- a missing failure status.

proposals.note:
This was the only proposal. It is taken whole, with five seams redesigned inside it:
- steps are isolated so a leftover window cannot satisfy a later step;
- step (c) targets a distinct 300-character deny-all folder instead of the file step (b) already revealed;
- the real-tree unit test gets an STA thread and a present-sibling control;
- the ACE is applied through the .NET ACL API and checked before the scan;
- the dialog watch is scoped to explorer.exe and the app, and the hook gets an explicit out-of-solution build.

It raised no over-engineering flag. Its product change is a deletion.
